{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "SecureShip",
          "organization": "SecureShip DevSecOps",
          "semanticVersion": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/secureship/secureship",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "SEC-000",
              "name": "Tracked Environment File (.env)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Tracked Environment File (.env)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The environment file '.env' appears to be tracked in version control, potentially leaking secrets."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The environment file '.env' appears to be tracked in version control, potentially leaking secrets.\n\nRemediation: Add .env files to .gitignore and provide a template .env.example with dummy values instead.",
                "markdown": "**Tracked Environment File (.env)**\n\nThe environment file '.env' appears to be tracked in version control, potentially leaking secrets.\n\n### Remediation\nAdd .env files to .gitignore and provide a template .env.example with dummy values instead."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SECRETS",
                "owasp": "A07:2021-Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-798",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SEC-002",
              "name": "Hardcoded GitHub Personal Access Token",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded GitHub Personal Access Token"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded GitHub personal access token detected. This could grant write or admin access to repositories."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Hardcoded GitHub personal access token detected. This could grant write or admin access to repositories.\n\nRemediation: Revoke the token immediately and inject it at runtime using GitHub Actions secrets or environment variables.",
                "markdown": "**Hardcoded GitHub Personal Access Token**\n\nHardcoded GitHub personal access token detected. This could grant write or admin access to repositories.\n\n### Remediation\nRevoke the token immediately and inject it at runtime using GitHub Actions secrets or environment variables."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SECRETS",
                "owasp": "A07:2021-Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-798",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SEC-001",
              "name": "Hardcoded AWS Access Key ID",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded AWS Access Key ID"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded AWS access key detected. An attacker can use this key to access cloud resources."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Hardcoded AWS access key detected. An attacker can use this key to access cloud resources.\n\nRemediation: Store the AWS credentials in environment variables (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID) or use AWS IAM Roles/AWS Secrets Manager.",
                "markdown": "**Hardcoded AWS Access Key ID**\n\nHardcoded AWS access key detected. An attacker can use this key to access cloud resources.\n\n### Remediation\nStore the AWS credentials in environment variables (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID) or use AWS IAM Roles/AWS Secrets Manager."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SECRETS",
                "owasp": "A07:2021-Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-798",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-009",
              "name": "Flask/Django Debug Mode Enabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Flask/Django Debug Mode Enabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Debug mode discloses detailed stack traces, internal configuration, and interactive debug consoles."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Debug mode discloses detailed stack traces, internal configuration, and interactive debug consoles.\n\nRemediation: Set DEBUG = False or load from environment variable (DEBUG = os.environ.get('DEBUG', 'False').lower() == 'true').",
                "markdown": "**Flask/Django Debug Mode Enabled**\n\nDebug mode discloses detailed stack traces, internal configuration, and interactive debug consoles.\n\n### Remediation\nSet DEBUG = False or load from environment variable (DEBUG = os.environ.get('DEBUG', 'False').lower() == 'true')."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-215",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-002",
              "name": "Command Injection via os.system",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Command Injection via os.system"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Direct invocation of os.system allows command injection if arguments are influenced by external input."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Direct invocation of os.system allows command injection if arguments are influenced by external input.\n\nRemediation: Use subprocess.run(['cmd', arg], shell=False) with an argument list instead of shell strings.",
                "markdown": "**Command Injection via os.system**\n\nDirect invocation of os.system allows command injection if arguments are influenced by external input.\n\n### Remediation\nUse subprocess.run(['cmd', arg], shell=False) with an argument list instead of shell strings."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A03:2021-Injection",
                "cwe": "CWE-78",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-003",
              "name": "Command Injection via subprocess shell=True",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Command Injection via subprocess shell=True"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "subprocess called with shell=True spawns a shell process vulnerable to argument injection."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "subprocess called with shell=True spawns a shell process vulnerable to argument injection.\n\nRemediation: Set shell=False and pass arguments as a list of strings: subprocess.run(['cmd', 'arg'])",
                "markdown": "**Command Injection via subprocess shell=True**\n\nsubprocess called with shell=True spawns a shell process vulnerable to argument injection.\n\n### Remediation\nSet shell=False and pass arguments as a list of strings: subprocess.run(['cmd', 'arg'])"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A03:2021-Injection",
                "cwe": "CWE-78",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-004",
              "name": "Insecure Deserialization via pickle",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Insecure Deserialization via pickle"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Deserializing untrusted data with pickle allows remote code execution via Python object reconstruction."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Deserializing untrusted data with pickle allows remote code execution via Python object reconstruction.\n\nRemediation: Use safe serialization formats such as JSON (json.loads) or Protocol Buffers.",
                "markdown": "**Insecure Deserialization via pickle**\n\nDeserializing untrusted data with pickle allows remote code execution via Python object reconstruction.\n\n### Remediation\nUse safe serialization formats such as JSON (json.loads) or Protocol Buffers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A08:2021-Software and Data Integrity Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-502",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-006",
              "name": "Dynamic Code Execution via eval/exec",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Dynamic Code Execution via eval/exec"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "eval() or exec() executes arbitrary code strings. Highly vulnerable if any argument is user-controlled."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "eval() or exec() executes arbitrary code strings. Highly vulnerable if any argument is user-controlled.\n\nRemediation: Refactor code to use dictionary lookups, ast.literal_eval, or specific safe parsers.",
                "markdown": "**Dynamic Code Execution via eval/exec**\n\neval() or exec() executes arbitrary code strings. Highly vulnerable if any argument is user-controlled.\n\n### Remediation\nRefactor code to use dictionary lookups, ast.literal_eval, or specific safe parsers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A03:2021-Injection",
                "cwe": "CWE-95",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-007",
              "name": "Use of Broken Cryptographic Hash (MD5/SHA1)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Use of Broken Cryptographic Hash (MD5/SHA1)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MD5 and SHA-1 have known collision weaknesses and should not be used for security-sensitive operations."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "MD5 and SHA-1 have known collision weaknesses and should not be used for security-sensitive operations.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade to SHA-256 (hashlib.sha256) or SHA-3/Argon2 for passwords.",
                "markdown": "**Use of Broken Cryptographic Hash (MD5/SHA1)**\n\nMD5 and SHA-1 have known collision weaknesses and should not be used for security-sensitive operations.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade to SHA-256 (hashlib.sha256) or SHA-3/Argon2 for passwords."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A02:2021-Cryptographic Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-327",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SAST-PY-008",
              "name": "Service Bound to All Interfaces (0.0.0.0)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Service Bound to All Interfaces (0.0.0.0)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Binding to 0.0.0.0 exposes the service to all network interfaces including public and untrusted networks."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Binding to 0.0.0.0 exposes the service to all network interfaces including public and untrusted networks.\n\nRemediation: Bind to 127.0.0.1 (localhost) or use a reverse proxy for external routing.",
                "markdown": "**Service Bound to All Interfaces (0.0.0.0)**\n\nBinding to 0.0.0.0 exposes the service to all network interfaces including public and untrusted networks.\n\n### Remediation\nBind to 127.0.0.1 (localhost) or use a reverse proxy for external routing."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SAST",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-200",
                "problem.severity": "note"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-COMPOSE-001",
              "name": "Privileged Container Execution",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Privileged Container Execution"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Container configured with privileged: true has full host device and kernel access, allowing container escapes."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Container configured with privileged: true has full host device and kernel access, allowing container escapes.\n\nRemediation: Remove privileged: true and grant only explicit Linux capabilities via cap_add if required.",
                "markdown": "**Privileged Container Execution**\n\nContainer configured with privileged: true has full host device and kernel access, allowing container escapes.\n\n### Remediation\nRemove privileged: true and grant only explicit Linux capabilities via cap_add if required."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-250",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-COMPOSE-002",
              "name": "Exposed Sensitive Service Port (5432)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Exposed Sensitive Service Port (5432)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Database / internal service port 5432 is bound to all host interfaces without loopback restriction."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Database / internal service port 5432 is bound to all host interfaces without loopback restriction.\n\nRemediation: Bind port to localhost only: '127.0.0.1:5432:5432' or use internal Docker network.",
                "markdown": "**Exposed Sensitive Service Port (5432)**\n\nDatabase / internal service port 5432 is bound to all host interfaces without loopback restriction.\n\n### Remediation\nBind port to localhost only: '127.0.0.1:5432:5432' or use internal Docker network."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-200",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SEC-006",
              "name": "High-Entropy API Key / Secret Assignment",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High-Entropy API Key / Secret Assignment"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "High-entropy secret or API key assignment detected via heuristic analysis."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "High-entropy secret or API key assignment detected via heuristic analysis.\n\nRemediation: Move secrets to an external configuration manager, environment variables, or a KMS.",
                "markdown": "**High-Entropy API Key / Secret Assignment**\n\nHigh-entropy secret or API key assignment detected via heuristic analysis.\n\n### Remediation\nMove secrets to an external configuration manager, environment variables, or a KMS."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SECRETS",
                "owasp": "A07:2021-Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-798",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-DOCKER-002",
              "name": "Unpinned Base Image Tag (:latest)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unpinned Base Image Tag (:latest)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Base image relies on unpinned or :latest tag, leading to unpredictable, non-reproducible builds."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Base image relies on unpinned or :latest tag, leading to unpredictable, non-reproducible builds.\n\nRemediation: Pin base image to an exact immutable version tag or SHA256 digest: FROM python:3.11.9-slim",
                "markdown": "**Unpinned Base Image Tag (:latest)**\n\nBase image relies on unpinned or :latest tag, leading to unpredictable, non-reproducible builds.\n\n### Remediation\nPin base image to an exact immutable version tag or SHA256 digest: FROM python:3.11.9-slim"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-1188",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-DOCKER-003",
              "name": "Sensitive Credential in Dockerfile ENV/ARG",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive Credential in Dockerfile ENV/ARG"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive environment variable or argument hardcoded in Dockerfile. Value persists in image metadata layers."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Sensitive environment variable or argument hardcoded in Dockerfile. Value persists in image metadata layers.\n\nRemediation: Use BuildKit secrets mount (RUN --mount=type=secret) or runtime environment injection.",
                "markdown": "**Sensitive Credential in Dockerfile ENV/ARG**\n\nSensitive environment variable or argument hardcoded in Dockerfile. Value persists in image metadata layers.\n\n### Remediation\nUse BuildKit secrets mount (RUN --mount=type=secret) or runtime environment injection."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A07:2021-Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "cwe": "CWE-798",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-DOCKER-001",
              "name": "Container Running as Root (Missing USER Instruction)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container Running as Root (Missing USER Instruction)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Dockerfile has no USER directive; container processes will run with root privileges inside the container."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Dockerfile has no USER directive; container processes will run with root privileges inside the container.\n\nRemediation: Create a dedicated unprivileged user and switch to it before ENTRYPOINT: RUN adduser -D appuser && USER appuser",
                "markdown": "**Container Running as Root (Missing USER Instruction)**\n\nDockerfile has no USER directive; container processes will run with root privileges inside the container.\n\n### Remediation\nCreate a dedicated unprivileged user and switch to it before ENTRYPOINT: RUN adduser -D appuser && USER appuser"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-250",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-K8S-001",
              "name": "Missing Pod Resource Limits (CPU/Memory)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing Pod Resource Limits (CPU/Memory)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Kubernetes containers without resource limits can cause Denial of Service (DoS) and starve neighboring workloads."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Kubernetes containers without resource limits can cause Denial of Service (DoS) and starve neighboring workloads.\n\nRemediation: Define resources.limits.cpu and resources.limits.memory for each container.",
                "markdown": "**Missing Pod Resource Limits (CPU/Memory)**\n\nKubernetes containers without resource limits can cause Denial of Service (DoS) and starve neighboring workloads.\n\n### Remediation\nDefine resources.limits.cpu and resources.limits.memory for each container."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-400",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IAC-K8S-002",
              "name": "Privileged Pod Security Context",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Privileged Pod Security Context"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod securityContext has privileged: true, allowing pod root to execute host operations."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Pod securityContext has privileged: true, allowing pod root to execute host operations.\n\nRemediation: Set privileged: false and drop unnecessary capabilities.",
                "markdown": "**Privileged Pod Security Context**\n\nPod securityContext has privileged: true, allowing pod root to execute host operations.\n\n### Remediation\nSet privileged: false and drop unnecessary capabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "IAC",
                "owasp": "A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration",
                "cwe": "CWE-250",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2024290",
              "name": "Open Redirect via malformed URLs in Express",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Open Redirect via malformed URLs in Express"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Express before 4.19.2 allows open redirection via mishandling user-supplied URL strings."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Express before 4.19.2 allows open redirection via mishandling user-supplied URL strings.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade express to version 4.19.2 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Open Redirect via malformed URLs in Express**\n\nExpress before 4.19.2 allows open redirection via mishandling user-supplied URL strings.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade express to version 4.19.2 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-601",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2020820",
              "name": "Prototype Pollution in lodash",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Prototype Pollution in lodash"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "lodash before 4.17.21 is vulnerable to prototype pollution in zipObjectDeep."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "lodash before 4.17.21 is vulnerable to prototype pollution in zipObjectDeep.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade lodash to version 4.17.21 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Prototype Pollution in lodash**\n\nlodash before 4.17.21 is vulnerable to prototype pollution in zipObjectDeep.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade lodash to version 4.17.21 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-1321",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2020281",
              "name": "Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) in axios",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) in axios"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Axios up to 0.21.1 is vulnerable to SSRF via follow-redirects proxy header bypass."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Axios up to 0.21.1 is vulnerable to SSRF via follow-redirects proxy header bypass.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade axios to version 0.21.2 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) in axios**\n\nAxios up to 0.21.1 is vulnerable to SSRF via follow-redirects proxy header bypass.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade axios to version 0.21.2 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-918",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2022235",
              "name": "Remote Code Execution in jsonwebtoken",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Remote Code Execution in jsonwebtoken"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Insecure key object validation allows arbitrary file write / code execution."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Insecure key object validation allows arbitrary file write / code execution.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade jsonwebtoken to version 9.0.0 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Remote Code Execution in jsonwebtoken**\n\nInsecure key object validation allows arbitrary file write / code execution.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade jsonwebtoken to version 9.0.0 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-502",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2021442",
              "name": "Log4Shell JNDI Remote Code Execution in Log4j",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Log4Shell JNDI Remote Code Execution in Log4j"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Apache Log4j2 JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker-controlled LDAP."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Apache Log4j2 JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker-controlled LDAP.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core to version 2.17.1 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Log4Shell JNDI Remote Code Execution in Log4j**\n\nApache Log4j2 JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker-controlled LDAP.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core to version 2.17.1 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-502",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2022229",
              "name": "Spring4Shell Remote Code Execution via Data Binding",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Spring4Shell Remote Code Execution via Data Binding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Spring Framework RCE via data binding on JDK 9+ when deployed as a WAR on Tomcat."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Spring Framework RCE via data binding on JDK 9+ when deployed as a WAR on Tomcat.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade org.springframework:spring-core to version 5.3.18 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Spring4Shell Remote Code Execution via Data Binding**\n\nSpring Framework RCE via data binding on JDK 9+ when deployed as a WAR on Tomcat.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade org.springframework:spring-core to version 5.3.18 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-94",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2023326",
              "name": "Unintended Leak of Proxy-Authorization in Requests",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unintended Leak of Proxy-Authorization in Requests"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Requests leaks Proxy-Authorization headers to destination servers when following redirects."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Requests leaks Proxy-Authorization headers to destination servers when following redirects.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade requests to version 2.31.0 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Unintended Leak of Proxy-Authorization in Requests**\n\nRequests leaks Proxy-Authorization headers to destination servers when following redirects.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade requests to version 2.31.0 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "SCA",
                "owasp": "A06:2021-Vulnerable and Outdated Components",
                "cwe": "CWE-200",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SCA-CVE2023438",
              "name": "Cookie Header Leak in urllib3 across Cross-Origin Redirects",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Cookie Header Leak in urllib3 across Cross-Origin Redirects"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "urllib3 does not remove HTTP Cookie headers during cross-origin redirect chains."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "urllib3 does not remove HTTP Cookie headers during cross-origin redirect chains.\n\nRemediation: Upgrade urllib3 to version 1.26.18 or higher.",
                "markdown": "**Cookie Header Leak in urllib3 across Cross-Origin Redirects**\n\nurllib3 does not remove HTTP Cookie headers during cross-origin redirect chains.\n\n### Remediation\nUpgrade urllib3 to version 1.26.18 or higher."
              },
              "properties": {
